Package: ggcarto
Title: Cartographic Class Intervals, Palettes and Bivariate Scales for 'ggplot2'
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person("Joel", "Capellan", email = "joelcapellan@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A single, consistent interface for color and fill scales in
    'ggplot2', built for thematic mapping. Brings together the class-interval
    algorithms used in cartography (quantile, natural breaks, Fisher, k-means,
    standard deviation, head/tails and more), a unified palette resolver that
    reaches 'grDevices', 'RColorBrewer', 'viridisLite', 'cols4all' and
    'paletteer', and map-oriented handling of limits, out-of-bounds squishing,
    transparency, interval labels and missing values. Every scale type --
    continuous, interval, categorical, ordinal and rank -- is reachable through
    one engine, so switching between them does not mean rewriting the call.
    Bivariate choropleths are supported end to end: classify two variables,
    colour them from an n-by-n palette grid, and draw the matching legend.
    Diagnostics make the decisions behind a map explicit and defensible:
    summarise and plot a classification, get a reasoned suggestion for the
    number of classes, check a palette for map use, and read every choice
    back off a finished plot.
